    {
      "id": "p-1",
      "type": "code",
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "title": "Worksheet: implement the hand fit",
      "statementHtml": "<p>Read n (1–100), n x/y pairs, and print slope and intercept to three decimals. Use slope zero for constant x.</p>",
      "hints": [
        "Return to centred sums if the denominator disappears."
      ],
      "solution": "practice/p-1.py",
      "tests": [
        {
          "stdin": "practice/p-1.t1.in",
          "output": "practice/p-1.t1.out"
        },
        {
          "stdin": "practice/p-1.t2.in",
          "output": "practice/p-1.t2.out"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p-2",
      "type": "code",
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "title": "Worksheet: evaluate a regressor",
      "statementHtml": "<p>Read n (1–100), n observed/predicted pairs, and print MAE MSE RMSE R2 to three decimals. Constant targets use undefined for R2.</p>",
      "hints": [
        "Compute target spread separately from residual magnitudes."
      ],
      "solution": "practice/p-2.py",
      "tests": [
        {
          "stdin": "practice/p-2.t1.in",
          "output": "practice/p-2.t1.out"
        },
        {
          "stdin": "practice/p-2.t2.in",
          "output": "practice/p-2.t2.out"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p-3",
      "type": "written",
      "difficulty": "hard",
      "title": "Worksheet: justify the chosen complexity",
      "statementHtml": "<p>A validation curve bottoms at degree four but degree twelve has lower training error. Which should you select?</p>",
      "hints": [
        "The clean rule does not override the observed validation comparison."
      ],
      "answerHtml": "<p>Choose degree four under the stated validation comparison, then assess the fixed choice on a separate final test. A finite validation winner can differ from a known generating degree.</p>"
    },
    {
      "id": "p-4",
      "type": "written",
      "difficulty": "hard",
      "title": "Worksheet: audit a housing claim",
      "statementHtml": "<p>A report says: our invented random-row rent score proves accuracy for every real Dhaka family. Identify the unsupported jumps.</p>",
      "hints": [
        "Separate synthetic arithmetic from population evidence."
      ],
      "answerHtml": "<p>Invented records cannot establish real market validity. A random-row average does not prove temporal transfer, unseen-building performance or equal error across families. Report the demonstrated split and obtain relevant real evaluation before broader claims.</p>"
    }
  ],
